# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Secrets — the ONLY secrets mechanism in this repo is
# playbooks/group_vars/all/secrets.yml. It is VAULT-ENCRYPTED AND LOCAL ONLY.
# One file, both environments. Credentials only; hostnames and API URLs live in
# the committed plaintext inventory/group_vars/<env>/connection.yml.
#
# IT USED TO BE COMMITTED, and untracking it in #130 is what makes this repo
# reusable. A public repo that ships one person's encrypted credentials hands a
# forker a blob they cannot decrypt, cannot replace without diverging from
# upstream, and that conflicts on every pull. secrets.yml.example is the
# contract now; the real file is built from it per machine.
#
# THE IGNORE RULE IS NOT THE SAFETY NET -- IT IS WHAT GETS CHECKED.
# utilities/check-no-secrets.sh verifies three things, none of which can pass
# silently: that this rule actually matches the file (git check-ignore), that
# nothing named secrets.yml is tracked, and that any tracked one is encrypted
# anyway. Deleting the rule below fails the build; it does not go unnoticed.
#
# The vault PASSWORD is the one secret that cannot be vaulted. It lives outside
# this repo at ~/secrets/.vault_pass_sales_demos (chmod 600, chmod 700 dir).
# The patterns below are belt-and-braces in case one is ever copied in here.
#
# Do NOT add a second sourceable secrets file (no docs/dev-environment.sh).
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# The real credentials file, and the example that documents its shape. The
# negation matters: without it the *.example twin would be swept up too, and
# that file is the only contract a new user has.
playbooks/group_vars/all/secrets.yml
!playbooks/group_vars/all/secrets.yml.example

.vault_pass
.vault_pass*
.vault_password
*.vault_pass
*.vault-password
.vault-password

# Kubeconfigs and cluster credentials
**/kubeconfig
*.kubeconfig
.kube/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Terraform — state can contain secrets in plaintext; tfvars almost always do.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.terraform/
.terraform.lock.hcl.bak
*.tfstate
*.tfstate.*
*.tfvars
*.tfvars.json
crash.log
crash.*.log
override.tf
override.tf.json
*_override.tf

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Ansible — collections are NEVER vendored into this repo. They install to the
# recommended path (Ansible's default ~/.ansible/collections) from the pinned
# collections/requirements.yml. Two artifact directories get created here and
# neither belongs in git:
#
#   collections/ansible_collections/  ansible-galaxy, if pointed at the repo
#   .ansible/                         ansible-lint's generated module mocks
#
# The .ansible/ mocks are regenerated from .ansible-lint `mock_modules` on
# every run, so tracking them only guarantees they go stale. (#8)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.retry
collections/ansible_collections/
!collections/requirements.yml
.ansible/

# Run logs belong in ~/ansible-logs, OUTSIDE this repo — it is public, and
# keeping them out entirely beats relying on a rule here. These patterns are
# only a guard in case someone points ANSIBLE_LOG_PATH at the working tree. (#26)
logs/
*.log

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Execution environment build artifacts (#31).
#
# utilities/build-ee.sh stages a COPY of ~/.ansible.cfg — which carries the
# Automation Hub token — into .ee-build/, because ansible-builder cannot read it
# from $HOME portably. That staged file is a real credential and must never be
# tracked. The generated build context lands under .ee-build/context/ too.
#
# .ee-build/ is deliberately NOT the repo root: an ansible.cfg at the root would
# shadow ~/.ansible.cfg and break certified collection installs machine-wide.
# Ansible does not look in subdirectories, so this location is inert.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.ee-build/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# NotebookLM staging (#64). utilities/collect-notebooklm-sources.sh copies the
# files named in utilities/notebooklm-sources.txt into build/notebooklm/ so
# they can be dragged into a browser. Every one of them is a COPY of a tracked
# file, so tracking the copies would only guarantee they go stale -- the same
# reasoning that keeps .ee-build/ out.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
build/

# Editor / OS
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
.DS_Store
__pycache__/
